    "body": "The new Rust component derives an affine basis from public linear equations, appends quadratic consequences, and retains every original variable and equation. A separate BigUint coefficient checker checks original-row lineage and each exact telescoping identity before admitting the output. This uses classical linear elimination; no generic algorithm novelty is claimed. Native PCC-20261116-313284, corrected shell interface PCC-20261116-503900, report PCC-20261116-1084a1; all unsigned/unverified. [pcc:unverified]\n\nAll 28 fixed curve inputs retain their before/after outcome classes and node counts: 13 original toy requests remain Unsupported, 13 indexed toy requests remain Root, and the two distinct actual-q1 inputs remain Root at eight nodes. The huge original/indexed actual-field inputs receive coefficient checks only, retaining 1059/1989 variables and producing 1174/2548 equations with 37/157 pivots, degree two, zero solver calls. Node counts are partial diagnostics; no time, complete-cost, live-memory or scaling conclusion follows. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe two-page [report](research/curve25519_torus_native_20261115/reports/affine-closure-v1/report.pdf), Markdown, editable pipeline, recorded-node plot/data, protocol, reproduction commands and all failed paths are included. The 64-input context is composite; old source/criteria/claim bytes remain unchanged. Both final PDF pages were inspected. Local release library controls/build/fmt/strict all-target Clippy pass, with exact source/binary/pre-call bindings. The corrected thin-shell round retains three positive and ten negative interface exits; historical Python-launched interface receipts stay unchanged and excluded from final interface acceptance. Two EOF advisories in pinned raw log/report Markdown are preserved; whole-diff whitespace is not called passing. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe complete 146256-byte raw archive is intentionally staged at its real policy-selected path for the maintained trusted artifact-autofix workflow. Local push found no AWS CLI, then no credentials after isolated CLI installation. Upload is pending: require a genuine subsequent manifest receipt for SHA-256 `ef5b561a184672f36ac9c2e12963f23d14d56aa731ea6e3d79f68968b3e2a875`, bytes146256, in `s3://setec-astronomy-artifacts/store`. No policy/exemption, workflow or credential change. See [PUBLISHING.md](research/curve25519_torus_native_20261115/affine-closure-v1/PUBLISHING.md). [pcc:unverified]\n\nThis is a separate touched-area lane stacked on #4447, whose actual current head has 31 checks and unresolved main journal/ledger conflicts. The parent branch is untouched; its one Copilot request remains pending. Do not merge this child into its feature parent to avoid main gates. After actual parent main integration, retarget to main, preserve the legitimate upstream policy update and all published histories, enable MERGE auto-merge and require the applicable fresh-head gates/reviews. Initial feature-base CI/review and artifact receipt are pending. Parent maintenance diagnostics PCC-20261116-6c4fce preserve the actual failures without waiving them. [pcc:unverified]\n\nSources checked: Shoup NTB v2 section14.4 pp388–391 and the repository's p256 auxiliary-smooth affine reducer; KB MCP/wrapper unavailable, Magma handbook401 and not read. Canonical cost/exponent charts and benchmarks are unchanged because this stage adds no admitted performance datum. Next is separately versioned branch-local certified reduction with rollback and full accounting, using the same public inputs/root order/caps; no such campaign is scheduled by the PR checker. Original-base discovery/yield/selection/kernel/recovery and signed/formal validation remain open. [pcc:unverified]\n",
